<Base title="Privacy notice" description="What HumAIn Logic collects (very little), why, and your choices.">
<section class="page-head"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Legal</span><h1>Privacy notice</h1><p class="confidence">Effective October 15, 2026</p></div></section>
<div class="container section" style="padding-top:var(--space-6)"><div class="prose">
<div class="callout warm" role="note"><strong>Draft, pending legal review.</strong> This notice describes how the site works today. It has not yet been reviewed by a lawyer and may change.</div>

<h2>In short</h2>
<ul>
<li>You don't need an account. We don't have accounts at all.</li>
<li>We don't use advertising cookies or tracking pixels, and we don't sell or share your data for advertising.</li>
<li>The only personal data we ask for is your email address, and only if you choose to get The Sunday Brief.</li>
<li>Searches, filters and job lookups run in your own browser. They are not sent to us.</li>
</ul>

<h2>1. Who we are</h2>
<p>HumAIn Logic (humainlogic.com) is an independent website run by Francisco Scaramanga in Rome, New York, USA. He is responsible for the personal data described here. See <a href="#contact">How to reach us</a>.</p>

<h2>2. What we collect and why</h2>
<h3>The Sunday Brief newsletter</h3>
<p>If you sign up, we collect your email address and the date you signed up. We use it only to send The Sunday Brief, one email a week on Sundays, and messages about your subscription. You must tick a box to agree, and you then confirm by clicking a link we email you (double opt-in). We don't ask for your name.</p>
<p>Our email provider, <a href="https://buttondown.com" rel="noopener">Buttondown</a>, stores your address and sends the emails for us. Buttondown may record technical details about the signup and whether emails are delivered or opened; see <a href="https://buttondown.com/legal/privacy" rel="noopener">Buttondown's privacy policy</a>.</p>
<p>Every email has a one-click unsubscribe link. When you unsubscribe, you stop getting emails right away and we keep your address only on a do-not-email list so we never mail you again by mistake.</p>
<h3>Visiting the site</h3>
<p>The site is hosted by <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare</a>. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes your IP address and basic request details (such as the page and browser type) to deliver pages and protect the site from abuse.</p>
<p>To count visits, we use or may use <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>. It does not use cookies, does not fingerprint you, and does not track you across other websites. It gives us totals such as page views and countries, not profiles of individual people.</p>
<h3>Things we don't collect</h3>
<p>We don't use cookies for tracking or ads. Fonts are served from our own site, not from Google. Your one setting, “Reduce motion”, is saved only in your browser.</p>
<h3>When you email us</h3>
<p>If you write to hello@humainlogic.com, we get your email address and whatever you include in the message. We use it only to reply and to fix or improve the site, and we delete messages we no longer need.</p>

<h2>3. Who we share data with</h2>
<p>Only the service providers above (Buttondown for email, Cloudflare for hosting and analytics), and only so they can provide their service to us. We don't sell your personal data, and we don't share it for cross-site advertising. We may disclose data if the law requires it.</p>

<h2>4. Links to other sites</h2>
<p>We link to AI tools, news sites and other resources. When you leave HumAIn Logic, the other site's privacy policy applies. Today the site has no affiliate links; if we add any, they will be labeled where you see them.</p>

<h2>5. How long we keep data</h2>
<p>We keep your email address while you're subscribed. After you unsubscribe, it stays only on the do-not-email list described above. You can ask us to delete it entirely.</p>

<h2>6. Your rights and choices</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Unsubscribe</strong> at any time with the link in any email.</li>
<li><strong>Access, correct or delete</strong> your data by contacting us. We will respond within 30 days.</li>
<li>Depending on where you live, such as California or the EU/UK, you may have more rights, like objecting to processing or complaining to your data protection authority. We will honor them.</li>
<li>We don't sell or share personal data, so there is nothing to opt out of. We don't treat you differently for using your rights.</li>
</ul>

<h2>7. Security</h2>
<p>The whole site uses HTTPS. We hold very little data, and the services that store it use industry-standard protections. If a breach affecting you ever happens, we will tell you as the law requires, including New York's SHIELD Act.</p>

<h2>8. Children</h2>
<p>HumAIn Logic is for adults. The newsletter is not meant for anyone under 16, and we don't knowingly collect data from children under 13. If you believe a child has signed up, contact us and we will delete it.</p>

<h2>9. International visitors</h2>
<p>We are based in the United States, and our providers may process data in the US and other countries.</p>

<h2>10. Changes</h2>
<p>If we change this notice, we will update the date at the top. If a change matters to subscribers, we will mention it in The Sunday Brief.</p>

<h2 id="contact">How to reach us</h2>
<p>Email <a href={mailto('Privacy question')}>hello@humainlogic.com</a>, or reply to any issue of The Sunday Brief.</p>
</div></div>
</Base>
